4. Clean rerun showed real drift, about six points down on multi-step tool tasks, consistent with the provider's model update from two weeks ago. While rerunning we watched for ⟦X⟧ given how much extra logging we bolted on to catch the caching bug, and sure enough the added instrumentation slowed things down enough to shift the ⟦TERM⟧ — much more front-loaded exploration than usual, like the agent was reacting to slower tool round-trips by hedging earlier.
5. ⟦TERM⟧ on the drifted tasks shifted too — much flatter now, less of the late-stage verification burn we used to see, which tracks with an agent that's less willing to double check itself before answering. Not sure if that's the update itself or if it's a downstream effect of the weaker recovery-without-notes behavior we saw in the yank pass.
